# Row Level Security

RLS is mandatory. Never rely on Flutter alone for access control.

## Driver Permissions

| Table | Access |
|-------|--------|
| profiles | Read/update own only |
| driver_documents | Read/upload own only |
| driver_days | CRUD own only |
| expenses | CRUD own only |

## Driver Restrictions

- Cannot read other drivers' data
- Cannot change `role` to admin
- Cannot set own `status` to approved
- Cannot approve own documents

## Admin Permissions

Full read on drivers, documents, driver_days, expenses, vehicles. Can approve/reject drivers and documents.

## Helper Pattern

Use a `is_admin()` SQL function checking `profiles.role = 'admin'` for admin policies. Driver policies use `auth.uid() = driver_id`.

```sql
-- Example: driver reads own days
CREATE POLICY "drivers_read_own_days" ON driver_days
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = driver_id);

-- Example: admin reads all
CREATE POLICY "admin_read_all_days" ON driver_days
  FOR SELECT USING (is_admin());
```

## Storage

All buckets private. Drivers upload to their own `{driver_id}/` prefix. Admins read via signed URLs.
